  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35733834",
      "title": "Defining Routes",
      "sourceHash": "d932addab1b4077ce466c0a5adf45015111569c56e25a30ea7672bc5c85419da",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.05,
          "en": "So these are the three steps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.05,
          "end": 6.36,
          "en": "And I'll of course start with step one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.36,
          "end": 9.51,
          "en": "and I'll start with it here in my root component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.51,
          "end": 11.253,
          "en": "in the App js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.18,
          "end": 14.67,
          "en": "And here we want to import something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.67,
          "end": 18.66,
          "en": "from that react-router-dom package, which we just installed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.66,
          "end": 21.24,
          "en": "And the something we wanna import here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.24,
          "end": 24.84,
          "en": "is the create browser router function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.84,
          "end": 27.54,
          "en": "This is a function provided by this package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.54,
          "end": 30.15,
          "en": "which allows us to define our routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.15,
          "end": 32.283,
          "en": "that we wanna support in this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.27,
          "end": 36.36,
          "en": "We call this function and to this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.36,
          "end": 40.83,
          "en": "we pass an array of route definition objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.83,
          "end": 43.98,
          "en": "So here we provide a couple of JavaScript objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.98,
          "end": 47.88,
          "en": "where every object represents one route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.88,
          "end": 50.31,
          "en": "And we add some properties to define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.31,
          "end": 52.68,
          "en": "the route characteristics like for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.68,
          "end": 56.28,
          "en": "the path for which this route should be activated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.28,
          "end": 58.41,
          "en": "By the way, there also is an alternative way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.41,
          "end": 59.73,
          "en": "of defining these routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.73,
          "end": 62.043,
          "en": "but for the moment let's start with this way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63,
          "end": 65.64,
          "en": "So here we define our route objects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.64,
          "end": 68.64,
          "en": "and these route objects take a couple of properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.64,
          "end": 71.46000000000001,
          "en": "with which we configure the routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.46000000000001,
          "end": 73.74,
          "en": "You should get decent auto completion here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.74,
          "end": 75.96000000000001,
          "en": "where you can see all these properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.96000000000001,
          "end": 77.31,
          "en": "and you can of course also learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.31,
          "end": 80.55,
          "en": "more about them here in the official documentation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 80.55,
          "end": 84.87,
          "en": "Now one key property, which you will almost always add,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.87,
          "end": 87.87,
          "en": "is the path property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.87,
          "end": 89.73,
          "en": "With that, you define the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.73,
          "end": 92.043,
          "en": "for which this route should be active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93,
          "end": 94.22999999999999,
          "en": "Now just to be clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.22999999999999,
          "end": 97.08,
          "en": "the path is the part after the domain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.08,
          "end": 100.41,
          "en": "So if you have a website like example.com,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 100.41,
          "end": 102.84,
          "en": "then this is your domain name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.84,
          "end": 106.44,
          "en": "and this is the protocol, this HTPs part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 106.44,
          "end": 110.61,
          "en": "But then thereafter, you have a path like slash products.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.61,
          "end": 114.06,
          "en": "Or maybe slash nothing if you're just on example.com.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.06,
          "end": 115.86,
          "en": "But either way, this is your a path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.86,
          "end": 120.86,
          "en": "Slash nothing is path, just as slash products is a path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.07,
          "end": 125.85,
          "en": "So that's the path here, the part after the domain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 125.85,
          "end": 129.66,
          "en": "And that is what we define here with the path property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.66,
          "end": 130.907,
          "en": "So we could, for example, say that this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.907,
          "end": 132.84,
          "en": "is the route for our main page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.84,
          "end": 134.79,
          "en": "for the starting page of this website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.79,
          "end": 138.27,
          "en": "and the path could therefore be slash nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.27,
          "end": 141.75,
          "en": "So if we are on our domain slash nothing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.75,
          "end": 144.9,
          "en": "then this route should be activated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.9,
          "end": 147.12,
          "en": "Now the second important piece of information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.12,
          "end": 150.12,
          "en": "we typically want to add to our route objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.12,
          "end": 152.22,
          "en": "is which component should be loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 152.22,
          "end": 154.38,
          "en": "when that route is active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 154.38,
          "end": 157.02,
          "en": "That's what I also mentioned before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.02,
          "end": 159.75,
          "en": "So therefore here we might want to add a new component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 159.75,
          "end": 163.56,
          "en": "and I'll add a folder named pages here to this project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.56,
          "end": 166.95,
          "en": "to hold the components that will be loaded as pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 166.95,
          "end": 168.57,
          "en": "by the router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 168.57,
          "end": 171.12,
          "en": "Now you don't have to name this folder pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 171.12,
          "end": 174.51,
          "en": "You can use the components folder you already know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.51,
          "end": 178.07999999999998,
          "en": "you could name it routes or whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 178.07999999999998,
          "end": 182.25,
          "en": "I just use separate pages folder with a name of pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 182.25,
          "end": 186.21,
          "en": "to clearly indicate that the components stored in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 186.21,
          "end": 189.24,
          "en": "whilst being regular React components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 189.24,
          "end": 191.343,
          "en": "will be loaded with help of Routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 192.3,
          "end": 195.36,
          "en": "So here we could then add a Home.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 195.36,
          "end": 198.72,
          "en": "that contains our homepage component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 198.72,
          "end": 203.1,
          "en": "which I of course want to export here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.1,
          "end": 206.04,
          "en": "And then in here I could add a title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 206.04,
          "end": 208.473,
          "en": "where I say my homepage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.49,
          "end": 211.92000000000002,
          "en": "So that's of course a very simple dummy component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 211.92000000000002,
          "end": 214.5,
          "en": "but it's good enough for the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.5,
          "end": 216.75,
          "en": "Now let's say we wanna load this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 216.75,
          "end": 218.67000000000002,
          "en": "when this route is active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 218.67000000000002,
          "end": 223.23,
          "en": "So if we're just on our domain.com/nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 223.23,
          "end": 225.99,
          "en": "Well to establish this connection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 225.99,
          "end": 228.03,
          "en": "we add another key property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 228.03,
          "end": 230.4,
          "en": "and that's the element property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 230.4,
          "end": 232.8,
          "en": "As the name adjusts with that property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 232.8,
          "end": 234.57,
          "en": "we define the element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 234.57,
          "end": 237.66,
          "en": "So in the end the JSX code that should be loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 237.66,
          "end": 239.613,
          "en": "when this path is active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 240.75,
          "end": 243.66,
          "en": "So for the element, you now define some JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 243.66,
          "end": 245.4,
          "en": "that should be rendered to the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 245.4,
          "end": 247.17,
          "en": "when this route is active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 247.17,
          "end": 250.68,
          "en": "In my case, that's the homepage component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 250.68,
          "end": 253.47,
          "en": "So I'm importing homepage from the pages folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 253.47,
          "end": 255.39,
          "en": "and the home component file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 255.39,
          "end": 258.42,
          "en": "And then here's the JSX code that should become active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 258.42,
          "end": 259.713,
          "en": "when this path is active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 260.58,
          "end": 262.86,
          "en": "Now you could have any JSX code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 262.86,
          "end": 265.86,
          "en": "You could add an extra paragraph that wraps this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 265.86,
          "end": 267.63,
          "en": "or do whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 267.63,
          "end": 271.56,
          "en": "But very often you will simply render a single component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 271.56,
          "end": 274.83299999999997,
          "en": "that then represents the entire page that should be loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 276.09000000000003,
          "end": 278.04,
          "en": "So these are now the first steps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 278.04,
          "end": 281.61,
          "en": "We created the route object with its path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 281.61,
          "end": 283.38,
          "en": "and we defined which component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 283.38,
          "end": 285.573,
          "en": "should be loaded when this route is active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 287.4,
          "end": 289.29,
          "en": "Now, before we're going to continue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 289.29,
          "end": 292.32,
          "en": "with more routes and more components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 292.32,
          "end": 295.59000000000003,
          "en": "let's stick to this single route here in this router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 295.59000000000003,
          "end": 298.65,
          "en": "and let's see how we can now use this router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 298.65,
          "end": 303.03,
          "en": "And to use it, we first of all must store the returned value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 303.03,
          "end": 305.67,
          "en": "of the create browser router function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 305.67,
          "end": 307.68,
          "en": "in a variable or constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 307.68,
          "end": 310.41,
          "en": "In this case, a constant called router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 310.41,
          "end": 314.7,
          "en": "We need this constant to then tell React that this router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 314.7,
          "end": 317.31,
          "en": "should be rendered to the screen, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 317.31,
          "end": 319.32,
          "en": "or that that router should be loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 319.32,
          "end": 323.25,
          "en": "and should render the appropriate pages to the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 323.25,
          "end": 326.101,
          "en": "And to tell React that this router should be used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 326.101,
          "end": 330.03,
          "en": "we need to import another thing from react-router-dom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 330.03,
          "end": 332.973,
          "en": "and that's the router provider component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 334.11,
          "end": 337.11,
          "en": "Now this component is a regular component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 337.11,
          "end": 339.9,
          "en": "which we can use like this in our JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 339.9,
          "end": 341.31,
          "en": "and we could of course again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 341.31,
          "end": 345.24,
          "en": "wrap it with other JSX code or add more JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 345.24,
          "end": 346.65,
          "en": "to this app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 346.65,
          "end": 350.25,
          "en": "But in this case, I'm only returning router provider.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 350.25,
          "end": 354.27,
          "en": "And this router provider component has a special prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 354.27,
          "end": 357.48,
          "en": "which we must set, the router prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 357.48,
          "end": 359.82,
          "en": "And the value we pass to the router prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 359.82,
          "end": 363.27,
          "en": "should be a router created with create browser router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 363.27,
          "end": 364.113,
          "en": "in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 364.98,
          "end": 369.303,
          "en": "So here I pass this router constant, to this router prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 370.23,
          "end": 371.37,
          "en": "And that's important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 371.37,
          "end": 375.87,
          "en": "this router constant is this value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 375.87,
          "end": 379.59,
          "en": "which is passed as a value for this router prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 379.59,
          "end": 380.943,
          "en": "That's how this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 381.9,
          "end": 386.76,
          "en": "And now with that, we're rendering the router on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 386.76,
          "end": 389.28,
          "en": "and we're activating the router, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 389.28,
          "end": 392.97,
          "en": "and the router will then, therefore, take a look at our url,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 392.97,
          "end": 395.55,
          "en": "see what the currently active path is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 395.55,
          "end": 397.68,
          "en": "and load the appropriate element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
